hostname r2
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.2/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to r1:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.12.2/30
!
interface Ethernet2
   description to r3:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.23.1/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON R2
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP
!   configure
!   router bgp 65002
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.2
!      neighbor 10.1.12.1 remote-as 65001
!      neighbor 10.1.23.2 remote-as 65003
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.1 activate
!         neighbor 10.1.23.2 activate
!         network 10.0.0.2/32
!      !
!
! NOTE: In EOS, received routes from neighbors are stored automatically.
!   You can always inspect pre-filter routes without any extra configuration:
!   show bgp neighbors 10.1.12.1 received-routes   ! what r1 sent (pre-filter)
!   show bgp neighbors 10.1.12.1 routes             ! what was accepted (post-filter)
!
! TASK 2 — Inbound prefix-list: block 172.16.2.0/24
!   ip prefix-list BLOCK-172-16-2 seq 5 deny 172.16.2.0/24
!   ip prefix-list BLOCK-172-16-2 seq 10 permit 0.0.0.0/0 le 32
!
!   router bgp 65002
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.1 prefix-list BLOCK-172-16-2 in
!      !
!
!   Apply: clear bgp neighbors 10.1.12.1 soft-inbound
!   Verify: show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   172.16.2.0/24 should be absent; 172.16.1.0/24 should be present.
!
!   Inspect pre-filter: show bgp neighbors 10.1.12.1 received-routes
!   Both /24s still appear here (raw from r1).
!   Post-filter: show bgp neighbors 10.1.12.1 routes
!   Only 172.16.1.0/24 appears.
!
! TASK 3 — More specific prefix-list matching
!   You can match a range of prefix lengths using "le" (less-than-or-equal)
!   and "ge" (greater-than-or-equal):
!
!   Block any prefix in the 172.16.0.0/16 space:
!   ip prefix-list BLOCK-172-16 seq 5 deny 172.16.0.0/16 le 32
!   ip prefix-list BLOCK-172-16 seq 10 permit 0.0.0.0/0 le 32
!
!   This matches 172.16.0.0/16 and ALL more-specifics up to /32.
!
! TASK 4 — Apply a route-map with prefix-list for more complex logic
!   A route-map can embed a prefix-list match and also set attributes:
!
!   ip prefix-list WANTED seq 5 permit 172.16.1.0/24
!
!   route-map FILTER-AND-TAG permit 10
!      match ip address prefix-list WANTED
!      set local-preference 150
!   route-map FILTER-AND-TAG deny 20
!      match ip address prefix-list BLOCK-172-16-2
!   route-map FILTER-AND-TAG permit 30
!
!   router bgp 65002
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.1 route-map FILTER-AND-TAG in
!      !
! ============================================================
end
